## VM arguments for ServiceRadar release
##
## These are passed to the Erlang VM when starting the release.
## See: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html

## Name of the node - configured via environment
## Use -name for fully qualified names (required for distributed cluster)
## Use -sname for short names (local development only)

## Async thread pool sized to the 2-core cpu quota (avoid CFS-oversubscribed I/O threads)
+A 2

## Increase process limit for large clusters
+P 1000000

## Increase port limit
+Q 65536

## Increase atom limit
+t 5000000

## Enable kernel polling for better network performance
+K true

## Cap schedulers to the cgroup cpu LIMIT (2 cores) and kill busy-wait spin.
## Baked here (not env) so it cannot be removed via ELIXIR_ERL_OPTIONS.
## NOTE: +sbt db removed — core-binding under CFS pins schedulers to cores the
## pod does not own, causing migration stalls.
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
+S 2:2
+SDcpu 2
+SDio 2

## Increase distribution buffer size for large messages
+zdbbl 32768

## Enable time warp mode for better time handling
+C multi_time_warp

## Garbage collection settings
+hms 8192
+hmbs 512
